IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nlca-dates`

-- Limitation Act 1981 (NT) -- the child abuse provisions: s 5A (no limitation period for child abuse actions) and
-- Part V Division 2, ss 53-55 (transitional matters for the Limitation Amendment (Child Abuse) Act 2017: earlier
-- judgments, settlements and pending actions). These are the Northern Territory's equivalents of the other Australian
-- jurisdictions' removal of limitation periods for child abuse claims and of their power to set aside earlier judgments
-- and settlements. The Territory's organisational liability for child abuse is in the Personal Injuries (Liabilities and
-- Damages) Act 2003 Part 3A, encoded beside that Act (see NOTES.md); nothing of it is restated here.
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in nlca-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and restates no rule. Nothing here
-- is exported. It is a second layer beside baseline-2026-11, which it neither imports nor changes.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "cannot", "may not", an
-- "if" or "where" that fails); NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment.
-- The court's judgments ("just and reasonable", whether a fair trial is possible) are inputs: the answer is conditional
-- on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Limitation Act 1981 (NT). Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is
-- owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the Northern Territory copyright policy of 8 October 1996; see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation Act 1981: child abuse`

§§ `The day fixed by the endnotes`

-- s 53(1): "commencement means the commencement of the Limitation Amendment (Child Abuse) Act 2017" -- 15 June 2017
-- (endnotes: "Commenced 15 June 2017 (Gaz S31, 15 June 2017)").
`the 2017 commencement` MEANS `the day` 15 6 2017

-- "before the commencement" (ss 54(1)-(3), 55(1)): a day strictly before 15 June 2017 (fork F3).
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day in question` `is before the 2017 commencement` IF `the day in question` `falls before` `the 2017 commencement`

§§ `s 5A(6) -- what child abuse is`

-- s 5A(6): "child abuse means any of the following perpetrated against a person when the person is (or was) under 18
-- years of age: (a) sexual abuse; (b) serious physical abuse; (c) psychological abuse that arises from abuse mentioned in
-- paragraph (a) or (b)." The three kinds are not defined in this Act: the kind is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Kind of conduct` IS ONE OF
    `sexual abuse`
    `serious physical abuse`
    `psychological abuse`
    `other harm or ill-treatment`

-- "under 18 years of age": a person born on a day is under 18 until the end of the day before the 18th birthday (F2).
GIVEN `the birth day` IS A DATE, `the day it was perpetrated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person was under 18 on` `the birth day` `the day it was perpetrated` IF
    `the day it was perpetrated` `falls before` (`the 18th birthday of a person born on` `the birth day`)

-- Paragraph (c): the psychological abuse must "arise from" sexual or serious physical abuse. Whose abuse it arises from
-- is not said (fork F1): asked as one fact, of anyone.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Kind of conduct`
      `it arose from sexual or serious physical abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5A(6)(a)-(c) -- the conduct is of a listed kind` `the conduct` `it arose from sexual or serious physical abuse` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `sexual abuse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `serious physical abuse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `psychological abuse` THEN `it arose from sexual or serious physical abuse`
    WHEN `other harm or ill-treatment` THEN FALSE

-- A "means" definition: JUST FALSE when it fails.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Kind of conduct`
      `it arose from sexual or serious physical abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the birth day` IS A DATE
      `the day it was perpetrated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5A(6) -- it is child abuse` `the conduct` `it arose from sexual or serious physical abuse` `the birth day` `the day it was perpetrated` MEANS
    IF      `s 5A(6)(a)-(c) -- the conduct is of a listed kind` `the conduct` `it arose from sexual or serious physical abuse`
        AND `the person was under 18 on` `the birth day` `the day it was perpetrated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 5A(1)-(4) -- the actions with no limitation period`

-- s 5A(1): "an action for damages for personal injury to a person arising from child abuse of the person". (3): "whether
-- the claim for damages is brought in tort, in contract, under statute or otherwise". (4): "extends to ... (a) a cause of
-- action that arises under the Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974; (b) a cause of action that survives on the death
-- of a person for the benefit of the person's estate under the Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1956."
DECLARE `Kind of action` IS ONE OF
    `my own action for damages for personal injury`
    `a family action under the Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 for the death of the person abused`
    `an action for the estate of the person abused, on a cause of action that survived the death`
    `an action that is not for damages for personal injury`

DECLARE `Effect of section 5A` IS ONE OF
    `no limitation period under this Act: the action may be brought at any time`
    `another Act's limitation period applies: this Act does not apply (s 5)`
    `section 5A does not apply: it was not child abuse as s 5A(6) defines it`
    `not decided by section 5A: the action is not one for damages for personal injury from child abuse`

-- s 5A(2): "Despite any other provision of this Act, an action mentioned in subsection (1) may be brought at any time and
-- is not subject to any limitation period under this Act." s 5: "This Act does not apply to any action for which a
-- period of limitation is prescribed by any other enactment". A period under another Act is not one "under this Act",
-- so s 5A(2) does not remove it, whichever way s 5 and "Despite any other provision" are read (finding 2).
-- The "means" definition failing gives the no; an action outside s 5A(1)'s own wording is NOTHING-kind (limited by its
-- own wording): the section is silent on it, and the Act's ordinary periods (encoded in baseline-2026-11) decide.
GIVEN `it is child abuse` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the action` IS A `Kind of action`
      `the injury or death arose from the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another Act sets a limitation period for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Effect of section 5A`
`s 5A -- the effect on my action` `it is child abuse` `the action` `the injury or death arose from the abuse` `another Act sets a limitation period for it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it is child abuse` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN `section 5A does not apply: it was not child abuse as s 5A(6) defines it`
        IF (`the action` EQUALS `an action that is not for damages for personal injury`) OR (NOT `the injury or death arose from the abuse`)
        THEN `not decided by section 5A: the action is not one for damages for personal injury from child abuse`
        IF `another Act sets a limitation period for it`
        THEN `another Act's limitation period applies: this Act does not apply (s 5)`
        OTHERWISE `no limitation period under this Act: the action may be brought at any time`

§§ `s 5A(5) -- the court's other powers`

-- s 5A(5): "This section does not limit: (a) any inherent jurisdiction, implied jurisdiction or statutory jurisdiction of
-- a court; or (b) any other powers of a court ..." Note: "this section does not limit a court's power to summarily
-- dismiss or permanently stay proceedings where the lapse of time has a burdensome effect on the defendant that is so
-- serious that a fair trial is not possible." The court's finding is an input. Where it finds a fair trial impossible,
-- s 5A does not stand in the way: JUST TRUE. Otherwise the powers come from outside this Act and the Act does not say
-- whether the court will use them (NOTHING-kind: points outside the text).
GIVEN `section 5A applies to my action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court finds a fair trial is not possible because of the lapse of time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5A(5) -- the court may still dismiss or stay for delay` `section 5A applies to my action` `the court finds a fair trial is not possible because of the lapse of time` MEANS
    IF `section 5A applies to my action` AND `the court finds a fair trial is not possible because of the lapse of time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Part V Division 2 -- earlier judgments, settlements and pending actions (ss 53-55)`

-- s 53(2): "a reference to a judgment given includes a judgment entered, and also extends to an agreement entered into in
-- relation to settlement of a matter of damages for personal injury to a person arising from child abuse of the person."
DECLARE `Earlier case` IS ONE OF
    `there was no earlier case`
    `a judgment that the limitation period had expired`
    `a judgment on legal professional negligence given on the ground that the limitation period had expired`
    `a judgment finally deciding the matter on other grounds`
    `a settlement agreement made because the claim was out of time`
    `a settlement agreement made for other reasons`
    `an action brought that had no judgment by 15 June 2017`

DECLARE `Where my earlier case leaves me` IS ONE OF
    `section 5A applies directly: no limitation period under this Act`
    `I may sue despite the earlier judgment, as if the earlier action had not been commenced`
    `section 5A removes the limitation period from my pending action`
    `I cannot sue again: a court finally decided the matter on other grounds before 15 June 2017`
    `the Act does not clearly say`
    `Part V Division 2 does not reach a judgment or settlement made on or after 15 June 2017`
    `Part V Division 2 does not reach it: the period was not one fixed by this Act or an Act it repealed`
    `not a child abuse action: Part V Division 2 is not read as reaching it`

-- s 54(1), (2) and, through s 53(2), a settlement: a judgment "given on the ground that a limitation period applying to
-- the cause of action had expired" (a settlement made because the claim was out of time, fork F4).
GIVEN `what happened` IS AN `Earlier case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `what happened` `is a judgment as mentioned in s 54(1) or (2)` IF
       (`what happened` EQUALS `a judgment that the limitation period had expired`)
    OR (`what happened` EQUALS `a judgment on legal professional negligence given on the ground that the limitation period had expired`)
    OR (`what happened` EQUALS `a settlement agreement made because the claim was out of time`)

-- s 53(1): "limitation period means a limitation period fixed by an Act repealed by this Act or fixed by or under a
-- provision of this Act (including a repealed provision of this Act)". A "means" definition: where the earlier judgment
-- applied another Act's period, ss 54 and 55 do not reach it (the no).
--
-- s 54(1): "An action may be brought after the commencement on a cause of action even if, before the commencement, a
-- judgment on the cause of action has been given on the ground that a limitation period applying to the cause of action
-- had expired." (2): the same for "a judgment in respect of legal professional negligence". (3): "However, an action
-- cannot be brought after the commencement on a cause of action where, before the commencement, a court had given
-- judgment in final determination of a matter on grounds other than that a limitation period applying to the cause of
-- action had expired." (4): "as if the action in which the previous judgment was given had not itself been commenced."
-- s 55(1): "an action brought before the commencement where: (a) before the commencement, a limitation period applied to
-- the cause of action; and (b) judgment had, at the commencement, not been given in the action." (2): "Section 5A
-- applies in relation to the action to remove the previously applying limitation period."
--
-- s 54 is read with its Division as reaching child abuse actions only (fork F5; finding 4). A settlement made for other
-- reasons before 15 June 2017 is neither "given on the ground" of the period nor plainly "a court had given judgment"
-- (NOTHING-kind: silent; fork F4). A judgment or settlement on or after 15 June 2017 is outside the Division's own
-- wording, "before the commencement" (NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording); s 5A itself then governs any new action.
GIVEN `it is a child abuse action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what happened` IS AN `Earlier case`
      `the day of the judgment or settlement` IS A DATE
      `the day the earlier action was brought` IS A DATE
      `the period was fixed by this Act or an Act it repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where my earlier case leaves me`
`ss 53-55 -- where my earlier case leaves me` `it is a child abuse action` `what happened` `the day of the judgment or settlement` `the day the earlier action was brought` `the period was fixed by this Act or an Act it repealed` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is a child abuse action`
    THEN `not a child abuse action: Part V Division 2 is not read as reaching it`
    ELSE CONSIDER `what happened`
         WHEN `there was no earlier case` THEN `section 5A applies directly: no limitation period under this Act`
         WHEN `an action brought that had no judgment by 15 June 2017` THEN `the pending action answer`
         OTHERWISE `the judgment answer`
    WHERE
        `the pending action answer` MEANS
            IF NOT (`the day the earlier action was brought` `is before the 2017 commencement`)
            THEN `section 5A applies directly: no limitation period under this Act`
            ELSE IF `the period was fixed by this Act or an Act it repealed`
                 THEN `section 5A removes the limitation period from my pending action`
                 ELSE `Part V Division 2 does not reach it: the period was not one fixed by this Act or an Act it repealed`
        `the judgment answer` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF NOT (`the day of the judgment or settlement` `is before the 2017 commencement`)
                THEN `Part V Division 2 does not reach a judgment or settlement made on or after 15 June 2017`
                IF `what happened` EQUALS `a judgment finally deciding the matter on other grounds`
                THEN `I cannot sue again: a court finally decided the matter on other grounds before 15 June 2017`
                IF `what happened` EQUALS `a settlement agreement made for other reasons`
                THEN `the Act does not clearly say`
                IF `the period was fixed by this Act or an Act it repealed`
                THEN `I may sue despite the earlier judgment, as if the earlier action had not been commenced`
                OTHERWISE `Part V Division 2 does not reach it: the period was not one fixed by this Act or an Act it repealed`

§§ `s 54(5)-(7) -- setting aside the earlier judgment, and what the court may take into account`

DECLARE `The court asked` IS ONE OF
    `the Supreme Court, hearing my new action`
    `the Supreme Court, on an application, not hearing my new action`
    `another court, hearing my new action`
    `another court, not hearing my new action`

DECLARE `Who gave the earlier judgment` IS ONE OF
    `the same court`
    `a different court`
    `no court: it was a settlement agreement`

-- s 54(5): "If an action is brought on or after the commencement, the court hearing the action may, if it considers it is
-- just and reasonable to do so, do any or all of the following: (a) set aside any judgment as mentioned in subsection
-- (1) or (2) already given on, or in relation to, the cause of action". (6): "The Supreme Court may, on application,
-- exercise the power under this section to set aside a judgment even though it is not hearing the action." (7): "A court
-- (other than the Supreme Court) may not exercise the power under this section to set aside a judgment of any other
-- court."
-- The power reaches only a judgment "as mentioned in subsection (1) or (2)", given before 15 June 2017: for anything else
-- s 54 gives no power and is silent on others (NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording). The "if" (just and reasonable)
-- and the "may not" of (7) give JUST FALSE. A court other than the Supreme Court not hearing the action is outside the
-- grant's own wording (NOTHING-kind). A settlement agreement is not "a judgment of any other court" (fork F6).
GIVEN `what happened` IS AN `Earlier case`
      `the day of the judgment or settlement` IS A DATE
      `the court asked` IS A `The court asked`
      `who gave it` IS A `Who gave the earlier judgment`
      `the court considers it just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54(5)(a), (6), (7) -- the court may set aside the earlier judgment` `what happened` `the day of the judgment or settlement` `the court asked` `who gave it` `the court considers it just and reasonable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`what happened` `is a judgment as mentioned in s 54(1) or (2)`)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the day of the judgment or settlement` `is before the 2017 commencement`)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `the court asked` EQUALS `another court, not hearing my new action`
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `the court considers it just and reasonable`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF (`the court asked` EQUALS `another court, hearing my new action`) AND (`who gave it` EQUALS `a different court`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `What the court may take into account` IS ONE OF
    `the damages and the costs`
    `the damages`
    `the costs`
    `nothing: no damages or costs were paid or are payable`
    `nothing: the court does not consider it just and reasonable`

-- s 54(5): "(b) take into account any amounts paid or payable by way of damages under such a judgment; (c) take into
-- account any amounts paid or payable by way of costs in connection with any action in which such a judgment was given."
-- Only "the court hearing the action" has these powers: (6) extends to the Supreme Court not hearing the action only "the
-- power ... to set aside a judgment". Outside a judgment as mentioned in (1) or (2), or for a court not hearing the
-- action, NOTHING (limited by its own wording).
GIVEN `what happened` IS AN `Earlier case`
      `the day of the judgment or settlement` IS A DATE
      `the court is hearing my new action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `damages were paid or are payable under it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `costs were paid or are payable in the earlier action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `What the court may take into account`
`s 54(5)(b), (c) -- what the court may take into account` `what happened` `the day of the judgment or settlement` `the court is hearing my new action` `damages were paid or are payable under it` `costs were paid or are payable in the earlier action` `the court considers it just and reasonable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`what happened` `is a judgment as mentioned in s 54(1) or (2)`)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the day of the judgment or settlement` `is before the 2017 commencement`)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `the court is hearing my new action`
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `the court considers it just and reasonable`
        THEN JUST `nothing: the court does not consider it just and reasonable`
        IF `damages were paid or are payable under it` AND `costs were paid or are payable in the earlier action`
        THEN JUST `the damages and the costs`
        IF `damages were paid or are payable under it`
        THEN JUST `the damages`
        IF `costs were paid or are payable in the earlier action`
        THEN JUST `the costs`
        OTHERWISE JUST `nothing: no damages or costs were paid or are payable`
